---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const app = 'https://github.com/albertoarena/sudo-play';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What sudoplay.dev loads, and what it does not. Google Analytics runs only if you accept, and no third party is contacted before that.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lead">This page is about this website, sudoplay.dev. The app has its own <a href={`${app}/blob/main/PRIVACY.md`}>privacy policy</a>, which says what Sudo Play sends and stores.</p>

  <h2>What this site loads</h2>
  <p>Every file on this site comes from sudoplay.dev: the pages, the styles, the icons and the font. The font, Geist Mono, is stored here. It does not come from a font service.</p>
  <p>Until you accept analytics, the pages make no request to a third party. There are no embedded videos, no maps, no social buttons and no search service.</p>
  <p>There is one small script. It adds the Copy button to code examples, and it sends nothing.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>This site uses Google Analytics to learn which pages are read, but only if you accept. Until you do, nothing from Google loads: not the script, and not a cookieless ping. If you decline, or ignore the question, Google is never contacted.</p>
  <p>Every advertising feature is switched off. This site has no advertising.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
  <p>Unless you accept analytics, this site sets no cookies. If you accept, Google Analytics sets its own cookies to tell repeat visits apart.</p>
  <p>Your choice is remembered in your browser's local storage, so you are not asked again. Local storage is not a cookie and is never sent to the server.</p>

  <h2>The server</h2>
  <p>Like any web server, the server that hosts this site sees the IP address that each request comes from. That is how a page reaches your browser.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Some links, like the ones to GitHub, take you to another website. That website's own privacy terms apply there.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Open an <a href={`${app}/issues`}>issue on GitHub</a>.</p>
</Base>
